hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1698","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn 'Abdah, narrated to us Hammad—meaning Ibn Yazid. Also narrated to us 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-'Ala', narrated to us Sufyan—both of them from Yahya. Also narrated to us 'Ali ibn Khashram, informed us Ibn 'Uyaynah, who said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed me, from 'Amrah, who said: I heard 'A'ishah (RA) say:

""If the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had seen what the women have innovated after him, he would have prevented them from the mosques just as the women of the Children of Israel were prevented.""

So I said: ""What is this? Were the women of the Children of Israel prevented?""

She said: ""Yes.""

This is the narration of 'Abd al-Jabbar.

In Ahmad's narration, he said: I said to 'Amrah: ""Were the women of the Children of Israel prevented?""

**CHAPTER:**"
